<title>USA: BankAtlantic says O'Neill resigned.</title>
<headline>BankAtlantic says O'Neill resigned.</headline>
<dateline>FORT LAUDERDALE, Fla. 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>BankAtlantic Bancorp said on Tuesday that John O'Neill resigned as president to pursue other opportunities in the industry.</p>
<p>The company appointed Chairman and Chief Executive Alan Levan to the additional position of president.</p>
<p>BankAtlantic, which is based in Fort Lauderdale, has assets of $2.7 billion and 56 branches statewide.</p>
<p>-- ((New York newsdesk 212-859-1611))</p>
